&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Pre-Sales Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, you are a &quot;developer-plus&quot; technical contributor. You are responsible for building high-quality mock backends, APIs, and demo infrastructure, but with a unique twist: you leverage &lt;strong&gt;LLMs and Generative AI&lt;/strong&gt; to prototype at high velocity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the critical boundary between Product Engineering and Go-to-Market. While you won&#39;t build production systems, you will build &quot;production-shaped&quot; assets: reusable, well-structured, and documented services that enable credible technical storytelling and high-fidelity client validation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your core responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Accelerated Prototyping: &lt;/strong&gt;Leverage LLMs (e.g., Claude and Gemini) to rapidly scaffold, build, and iterate on proof-of-concept apps and mock services. You move faster than a traditional sprint by using AI to handle the &quot;heavy lifting&quot; of boilerplate and logic generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Asset Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Design, build, and maintain reusable mock services in Node.js / TypeScript. You’ll implement contract-first APIs (REST/GraphQL), manage AWS deployments (API Gateway, Containers), and handle persistence using PostgreSQL or DynamoDB&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure as Code: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage demo environments using Terraform, ensuring environments are reproducible and secure using existing OIDC authentication patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with frontend engineers to ensure UI components point cleanly to your mock services, debugging integration issues and supporting end-to-end demo flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Pre-Sales Support: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with Pre-Sales consultants to translate client &quot;win themes&quot; into working technical artefacts. You will occasionally demo directly to clients, showcasing how Kaluza solves their specific retail challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; UX Influence: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate with Design and Product teams for UI direction while developing your own design ideas to make Kaluza’s capabilities shine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentorship &amp;amp; Standards: &lt;/strong&gt;Set informal engineering standards for the pre-sales team, mentoring others on API design and architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Evangelism:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the resident expert in GenAI workflows for the Commercial team, mentoring others on how to use AI to bridge the gap between &quot;slide-ware&quot; and &quot;software.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What this role is NOT:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pure presentation-led role (you will be writing code regularly).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipping production code (your value comes from building things that&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;work&lt;/em&gt; for a demo, not maintaining production SLOs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
