&lt;p class=&quot;section-title&quot;&gt;As a Senior Producer, you are responsible for the effective management and delivery of projects, ensuring the best creative&lt;br&gt;solutions across a designated portfolio of clients are achieved in the most efficient, profitable and imaginable way for the Studio&lt;br&gt;while managing client expectations accordingly. You will be expected to lead production projects and delivery at Made Thought,&lt;br&gt;as the go-to in the team for Production led projects. You will play a vital role in building and nurturing relations with key industry&lt;br&gt;players, alongside lead creative, producing large productions on time and on budget. You must be creatively minded, and&lt;br&gt;understand how to carefully balance the flexibility required of a business with creativity at it’s core, alongside the rigour and strong&lt;br&gt;organisational skills which some of our clients can expect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;section-title&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;section-title&quot;&gt;— Work collaboratively with the Creative team to actively ensure the best creative solutions are delivered against each client&lt;br&gt;brief. You will have the abilitiy to motivate people around you; both colleagues and clients, earning their trust and confidence.&lt;br&gt;— Run and manager a number of projects in the studio totalling circa £1-£1.5M per annum (inc third party productions costs).&lt;br&gt;You will be responsible for the allocation, planning and forecasting of all projects within your portfolio, ensuring they are set&lt;br&gt;up for the success from the outset.&lt;br&gt;— Be the key point of contact from Made Thought for all third parties related to the production process.&lt;br&gt;— Create a presence within the industry to ensure talent are keen to work with Made Thought and be actively seen as the&lt;br&gt;escalation point for production queries or issues within Made Thought.&lt;br&gt;— Be accountable for production project budgets and timings, ensuring the project is delivered on time to budget maintaining&lt;br&gt;an agreed project margin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;section-title&quot;&gt;— Utilising previous experience to think creatively and fluidly when providing solutions, escalating issues to Account Director or&lt;br&gt;Client Services when needed.&lt;br&gt;— Project dependent, support the Account Director (project lead) on larger / more complex projects to ensure all aspects of the&lt;br&gt;day-to-day are executed efficiently and effectively.&lt;br&gt;— Work with the Resource and Creative team to ensure the right team and timeline are in place. You will approach this&lt;br&gt;sensitively and intelligently to allow for profitability whilst protecting the creative process.&lt;br&gt;— Be accountable for your project commercials, with the ability to accurately scope, plan and deliver your projects on time,&lt;br&gt;working closely with the Finance Team to ensure projects are delivered on budget.&lt;br&gt;— Set and manage production budgets, to then provide weekly project status and cost reporting to the Finance and Client&lt;br&gt;Services Director.&lt;br&gt;— Forecasting production workflow for the upcoming quarter for your projects, highlighting any potential overruns before they&lt;br&gt;occur and proactively working with the team to reduce them.&lt;br&gt;— Conduct project wash-ups, sharing relevant findings with the wider team, and owning any improved ways of working&lt;br&gt;identified.&lt;br&gt;— Build strong and lasting relationships with our clients, maintaining regular contact to keep them updated on overall project&lt;br&gt;progress, highlighting any potential delays or scope for overspend. You will respond with speed and assurance to their&lt;br&gt;requests.&lt;br&gt;— Support new business on writing proposals and casting a team to suit your projects. You will also be accountable for creating&lt;br&gt;proposals from scratch (dependant on project size), seeking approval from Account Director where required.&lt;br&gt;Safeguard internal processes that protect Made Thought’s unique culture and creative output, while consistently looking for&lt;br&gt;and contributing towards improved processes and ways of working for the team.&lt;br&gt;— Research, suggest and inform the project team of which third parties should be used for the concept and will creatively&lt;br&gt;challenge in alignment with Made Thought’s creative ambition and budget / usage guidelines.&lt;br&gt;— Be accountable for ensuring usage rights are agreed and flagging when a touch point is approaching the end of a usage&lt;br&gt;period, negotiating extended usage accordingly.&lt;br&gt;— Use comprehensive knowledge of copyrights legislation on usage rights, and seek updated rules that govern usages to&lt;br&gt;ensure the company’s practices meets these standards.&lt;br&gt;— Oversee image checks, crediting, picture quality, repro for online and offline formats.&lt;br&gt;— Source new talent and production partners, build, update and maintain a MT production bank (including photographers,&lt;br&gt;directors, models, locations, studios, glam and set teams, and suppliers).&lt;br&gt;— Build strong relationships between Made Thought and shoot production industry (ie. Agents, production companies,&lt;br&gt;photographers, set designers and stylists).&lt;br&gt;— Manage and arrange commissioning of pre-existing assets from stock imagery to music, negotiating and agreeing usage as&lt;br&gt;necessary.&lt;br&gt;— Collaborate with internal creative team (AD / DD) to present relevant AD decks to clients throughout the production process&lt;br&gt;– ensuring creative expectations are in line / within client budget and overall scope of production.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;section-title&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;section-title&quot;&gt;SKILLS &amp;amp; EXPERIENCE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;section-title&quot;&gt;— A rich portfolio of client relationships across multiple sectors, with proven experience of successfully nurturing and growing&lt;br&gt;client relationships.&lt;br&gt;— The ability to work seamlessly with others, leading by example and getting stuck in where needed.&lt;br&gt;— Bring demonstrable experience in developing and motivating teams, supporting people to reach their potential.&lt;br&gt;— Be able to balance the big picture with the detail, being able to think ahead and prioritse the workload for both yourself and&lt;br&gt;the team.&lt;br&gt;— Be a strong problem solver who does so with diplomacy and charm, and who considers the best outcomes for both client &amp;amp;&lt;br&gt;agency.&lt;br&gt;— Have the ability to build trust within teams and inspire others.&lt;br&gt;— Exceptional standard of written and oral communication.&lt;/p&gt;
